<title>SYRIA: Syria buys 13,000 T raw sugar at $296.6.</title>
<headline>Syria buys 13,000 T raw sugar at $296.6.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Syria's General Foreign Trade Organisation for Chemicals and Foodstuffs (GEZA) on Thursday bought 13,000 tonnes of raw sugar at $296.6 per tonne, a GEZA spokesman said.</p>
<p>He told Reuters the sugar, bought from France's Lorico, should be delivered in April.</p>
<p>He said a tender to buy 13,000 tonnes of white sugar was cancelled as price offers did not meet GEZA conditions.</p>
</text>
